    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d416">

                <pb facs="0508" n="410" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg410"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/763</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs at Nanking to
                        the Chinese Legation</hi><anchor n="58" xml:id="d416-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-12-10">December 10, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Marshal Chang Hsiao-Liang reported by wire that, between September 18, 1931 and
                    December 5, 1932, there were about fifty-eight thousand two hundred and
                    forty-eight (58248) men killed in the Three Eastern Provinces, among those
                    twelve thousand and twenty-six (12026) were civilians of the Provinces, twenty
                    thousand two hundred and fourteen (20214) were Government troops, three hundred
                    and ninety (390) were policemen, and twenty-five thousand six hundred and
                    eighteen (25618) were volunteer forces. These people met their death in various
                    ways. They were either executed, shelled, bombed, burned, buried alive,
                    bayoneted, cut or chopped by knives, soaked with petroleum and burned,
                    strangled, thrown into wells and drowned, or killed in other cruel ways.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
